  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1200 PM CDT Wed Jul 22 2026\n\nToday through Friday...\n\nHigh pressure in southern MN will slide southeast today and\ngradually slide east across the southern Great Lakes region \ntonight through Thursday. The core of the surface high will\nshift to the NE US but the high pressure will extend much\nfurther west across WI. In the upper levels we will remain in\nbetween the ridge to the west and trough to the east. While\nthere should be some activity aloft with various shortwaves the\nconditions will be much too dry for anything to come of the \nupper level forcing.\n\nThe high pressure will finally start to exit Friday with lower \npressure pushing in from the west as the ridge aloft nudges \ntoward the region. No real weather concerns for this period as \nwe remain dry.\n\nFriday night through Wednesday...\n\nAs the ridge slides into the region this weekend expect\ntemperatures to warm back up with a return of humid conditions,\nbut also a return of precip/storm chances. Saturday will carry \nminor chances across northern WI late Friday night into the day \nSaturday with a weak embedded shortwave sliding down the ridge.\nThere currently looks to be enough moisture and forcing to bring\nsome precip with some instability in the region likely allowing\nfor some storms as well. While timing is not exactly great for\nstronger storms there is enough shear present to perhaps bring a\nfew stronger storms so its worth monitoring. \n\nSunday and Monday will be warmer with highs in the upper 80s to\nlow 90s with multiple chances for storms though the best chance\nfor strong to severe storms appears to be Sunday \nafternoon/evening where WAA and a warm front as the primary \nforcing should allow for high instability and a decent LLJ will\nbring in enough shear to bring some severe weather concerns.\nOtherwise increased uncertainty into early next week but\neventually we will see a front push through and cool the region\noff a tad but since the ridge remains in place we should\ncontinue to expect warm conditions. Later next week the ridge\nmay revert back west a bit and allow .\n\nIt is worth mentioning that Beach Hazards Statement may be\nneeded for Friday as breezy onshore winds may yield nearshore\nwave heights from 3-5 feet.",
